Port of the RTL8188CU eFuse read/power sequence and compact ROM decoding
from OpenBSD rtwn.c revision 1.61 (2025-08-20), for Panther.
Register/ROM layout: r92creg.h. Firmware selection: if_urtwn.c.
Changes: checked I/O, bounds, explicit endian access, rollback and validation.

Version 0.3.0 ports the RTL8188CU USB power-on, 8051 reset and firmware
page upload/start sequences from the same rtwn.c and if_urtwn.c references.
The boot probe keeps host data paths disabled and quiesces the MCU afterward.

Version 0.4.0 adds the board-0/TSMC/1T1R MAC, BB, AGC and RF tables from
r92creg.h, plus RF access, IQ/LC calibration and PA-bias sequences from rtwn.c
and if_urtwn.c. Adaptations: checked USB operations, restricted hardware scope,
full temporary IQ snapshots/restoration, all-component signed IQ comparison,
portable signed fixed-point arithmetic, bounded LC polling, disabled data paths
and quiescence before releasing USB. No net80211 stack is included.

Version 0.5.0 ports LLT/DMA queue setup from urtwn_dma_init/urtwn_llt_init.
All 256 links are read back; both MAC clocks are enabled for RX, with TX DMA
disabled and all TX queues paused. DMA aggregation uses urtwn_aggr_init's
threshold and timeout. No OUT frame is submitted. The original
bounded parser in rx.c uses the USB descriptor layout and aggregate alignment
from r92creg.h/urtwn_rxeof; it counts CRC-verified beacons without retaining
frame contents. The Panther asynchronous USB backend is original project code.

Version 0.8.0 adds the board-0/TSMC/1T1R, 20 MHz TXAGC calculation and
packing from rtwn_r92c_get_txpower/rtwn_write_txpower, CCMP CAM word layout
from rtwn_set_key/delete_key, and the USB TX descriptor from if_urtwn.c.
Adaptations: explicit byte encoding, readback/bounded busy polling, invalidation
before replacement, verified erasure on failure, and power-register rollback.
The descriptor builder is limited to management/EAPOL at CCK1, with software
sequence numbers and explicit USB ZLP requirements. No USB OUT backend exists.
The opt-in hardware probe uses public synthetic keys and clears all CAM entries
before allowing passive RX; all TX queues remain paused and TXDMA is disabled.
